# ── Associations for which no evidence was located ───────────────────────────
#
# Recorded rather than deleted. Each says what was claimed, that nothing
# supporting it was found in this corpus, and on what date — which is the
# knowledge the old scope notes destroyed by stating the association flatly.

<https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/evidence/delta-down-regulation/status/1>
    a sstim-ex:KnowledgeStatusAssertion ;
    rdfs:label "Scoped knowledge-status assertion for deltaOscillation and heavy down-regulation (noKnownEvidenceInSSTIM)"@en ;
    sstim-ex:hasKnowledgeStatus sstim-ex:noKnownEvidenceInSSTIM ;
    sstim-ex:knowledgeAsOfDate "2026-08-15"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/evidence/delta-down-regulation/status/1/activity> ;
    sstim-ex:knowledgeScopeNote "No source was located characterising delta activity as heavy down-regulation. The phrase has no standard referent in the electrophysiology literature, and delta's association with slow-wave sleep is recorded instead as an observation condition on the concept, not as an outcome. Asserted in the sstim-v:delta scope note until ADR 0049 moved it here. This is a statement about the BSC Lab curated SSTIM corpus as of this date, not a universal claim about the world."@en .

sstim-v:deltaOscillation sstim-ex:hasKnowledgeStatusAssertion <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/evidence/delta-down-regulation/status/1> .

<https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/evidence/theta-creativity/status/1>
